gal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Stifle","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","oracle_text":"Counter target activated or triggered ability. (Mana abilities can't be targeted.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2014-06-06","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":["Devoid"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}{R}","name":"Turn Against","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","oracle_text":"Devoid (This card has no color.)\nGain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2015-10-02","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If lethal damage is dealt to a creature with an enrage ability, that ability triggers. The creature with that enrage ability leaves the battlefield before that ability resolves, so it won't be affected by the resolving ability.","oracle_id":"2a86b70b-34ca-45df-8aa1-c3fb2da72dc3","published_at":"2018-01-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple sources deal damage to a creature with an enrage ability at the same time, most likely because multiple creatures blocked that creature, the enrage ability triggers only once.","oracle_id":"2a86b70b-34ca-45df-8aa1-c3fb2da72dc3","published_at":"2018-01-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If more than one creature damages it at one time, it only gets one counter.","oracle_id":"3e771f5b-2de3-4a1b-8281-ab1f7491e5a1","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Boros Reckoner's first ability will trigger even if it is dealt lethal damage. For example, if it blocks a 7/7 creature, its ability will trigger and Boros Reckoner will deal 7 damage to the target.","oracle_id":"5f079a75-899e-467d-b443-3b87ce2fb548","published_at":"2017-03-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Damage dealt by Boros Reckoner due to its first ability isn't combat damage, even if it was combat damage that caused that ability to trigger.","oracle_id":"5f079a75-899e-467d-b443-3b87ce2fb548","published_at":"2017-03-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Boros Reckoner is dealt damage by multiple sources at once, such as by two creatures blocking it, its ability triggers once and one target is dealt that much damage.","oracle_id":"5f079a75-899e-467d-b443-3b87ce2fb548","published_at":"2017-03-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A card with devoid is just colorless. It’s not colorless and the colors of mana in its mana cost.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Cards with devoid use frames that are variations of the transparent frame traditionally used for Eldrazi. The top part of the card features some color over a background based on the texture of the hedrons that once imprisoned the Eldrazi. This coloration is intended to aid deckbuilding and game play.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Devoid works in all zones, not just on the battlefield.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn’t cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card loses devoid, it will still be colorless. This is because effects that change an object’s color (like the one created by devoid) are considered before the object loses devoid.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Other cards and abilities can give a card with devoid color. If that happens, it’s just the new color, not that color and colorless.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn Against can target any creature, even one that’s untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"634d6357-af76-4e25-8c63-81522bc726f5","published_at":"2015-08-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If lethal damage is dealt to a creature with an enrage ability, that ability triggers. The creature with that enrage ability leaves the battlefield before that ability resolves, so it won't be affected by the resolving ability.","oracle_id":"80bb9ce4-1f3c-42ca-b75f-9a6b2f42073b","published_at":"2018-01-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple sources deal damage to a creature with an enrage ability at the same time, most likely because multiple creatures blocked that creature, the enrage ability triggers only once.","oracle_id":"80bb9ce4-1f3c-42ca-b75f-9a6b2f42073b","published_at":"2018-01-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.","oracle_id":"b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
